From 8fe885595eb72fbdeede3abc49337a228d91b29f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fluorite Integration Role
Date: Mon, 9 Mar 2026 01:05:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] layout: fall back to default output before background exists

Upstream-Status: Pending

For the fluorite NORMAL path we now reach DESKTOP role assignment, but startup
still aborts if no background surface has been registered yet. In that case the
compositor raises a protocol error even though a real output already exists.

Prefer the current output, then the background output, and finally the default
compositor output before aborting. This keeps NORMAL startup alive while the
background is still catching up during boot.
---
 src/layout.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layout.c b/src/layout.c
index 7ef8adf..466f14b 100644
--- a/src/layout.c
+++ b/src/layout.c
@@ -642,6 +642,14 @@ ivi_layout_desktop_committed(struct ivi_surface *surf)
 		if (!r_output)
 			r_output = ivi_layout_find_bg_output(surf->ivi);
 
+		/* if the background is not up yet, still use a real output */
+		if (!r_output) {
+			struct weston_output *woutput =
+				get_default_output(surf->ivi->compositor);
+			if (woutput)
+				r_output = to_ivi_output(woutput);
+		}
+
 		/* if we couldn't still find an output by this point, there's
 		 * something wrong so we abort with a protocol error */
 		if (!r_output) {
